{
	"_comment": "The Exchange: townsfolk post bounties in the paper. Each request's 'per' is the vanilla villager trade range in items (or creatures) per emerald: [base, base with demand]. The rate used is drawn from that range, skewed towards the base by 'skew', so bounties pay at the generous end of vanilla prices; quantities are a week's worth. 'tier' is how far along a player must be: 0 starting out, 1 has found iron, 2 has been to the Nether, 3 has been to the End. 'pays' lists what a character may pay in besides emeralds, with each item's emerald value (vanilla selling prices). Names and towns come from names.json; 'id' picks the profession's name list. Each reader gets 'deliveries' notices from different trades and 'slayings' jobs for the Watch. A 'pays' item's 'stack' is how many fit in one stack when that isn't 64.",
